Driver for Ezi-Servo 2 Plus-E controller
=======================================

Rea Domitrović <redomitro@irb.hr> July 2026

Introduction
------------

This is a Model 3 (asynMotor) FASTech Ezi-Servo 2 Plus-E (EzS2PE) controller by implementing methods 
from the asynMotorController and asynMotorAxis classes. Communication is established over Ethernet via 
the UDP protocol for reduced overhead versus TCP.

Overall communication is achieved using octets, but they are not ASCII-compatible strings; the EzS2PE 
controller takes binary data as input. For that reason, the asynMotorController::writeReadController 
method had to be overriden to make everything work as expected.

Velocity and acceleration
-------------------------

Leaving VELO/JVEL fields at 0 will cause the motor to move at 50000 steps per second. The actual 
speed in rpm will depend on the type of motor you have.

If using motor version 7-4 or earlier, or master before 2026-07-30: If HVEL is left as 0, the motor 
record defaults to setting HVEL=VBAS. To instead make HVEL mirror VBAS, apply the provided patch file 
(hvelPatch.patch) in your motor module top directory.

If acceleration is left unset, the record will drive the device with accelerations of 0.1 seconds for 
all movements. If ACCL is set, jog acceleration will mirror move/tweak acceleration on IOC startup, but 
not if ACCL/ACCS is set via channel access. This can cause jog and move accelerations to become 
desynced.

IOC setup
---------

Ezi-Servo 2 Plus-E uses TCP on port 2001 or UDP on port 3001 to communicate. To set up the motor in the 
IOC using UDP, the following lines need to be added to your st.cmd:

drvAsynIPPortConfigure(<portName>, "<ipAddress>:3001 UDP", 0, 0, 1)
EzS2PECreateController(<motorName>, <portName>, 1, <movingPollPeriod>, <idlePollPeriod>, 0)

The poll communication has quite a bit of overhead - the motor returns 38 bytes - so reducing the poll 
rate to avoid eating too much bandwidth can be considered.

In drvAsynIPPortConfigure, it is important that the last argument (noProcessEos) be set to 1. The 
controller doesn't use a standard message terminator (EOS) and instead hardcodes the length of a 
message, so it is necessary to disable EOS processing. The UDP argument can be left out if you want to 
use TCP, but in that case set the port to 2001 instead.

Restrictions
-----------

This driver does not support all features of the Ezi-Servo controller, many of which are outside the 
motor record anyway.

To my knowledge, the controller can only independently control one axis; there is nothing in the 
communication spec that allows for axis addressing. If multiple axes are connected, they will all 
perform the same commands.

Currently autosave functionality is not implemented.
